# @PROJECT_NAME@

Your first Game Boy Color ROM shows the project name with three looping gold sparkles. Open `build/game.gbc` in a Game Boy Color emulator.

## Edit and rebuild

1. Connect VS Code to the Docker host if you work remotely. Open this project's folder and select **Dev Containers: Reopen in Container**.
2. Open `src/main.c`. Change the title or start adding your game after the animation.
3. Run `make` in the VS Code terminal or choose **Terminal → Run Build Task**. Reload `build/game.gbc` in your emulator.

You can also rebuild from the host terminal in this directory.

```sh
docker compose up -d
docker compose exec -T dev make
```

Use `docker compose down` from this folder to remove the container. Your source, Git history, and ROM stay here. To play on another computer, copy or download `build/game.gbc` from the host and open it in your emulator. You can save revisions with Git and share the ROM as a release asset when it's ready.

Use HTTPS Git remotes inside the container. For a Git remote that uses SSH, run Git in the host checkout with your host's SSH client and keys.
